. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H3 * (
. 
.         * Description:
.         * Again, we assume that nature randomly assigns the gender of childre
> n and based on the subset
.         * of households who became parents (unobserved variables might drive 
> the decision to become a parent
.         * in the first place), we estimate the effect of one additional daugh
> ter on the share of childcare
.         * fathers take over on weekends (i.e., Staturday and Sunday).
.         * Additionally, we include control variables for income and employmen
> t status of mother and father, respectively, as well as household fixed effec
> ts. Finally,
.         * we use cluster robust standard errors on the household level.
. 
. 
